---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base title="Licence — Matra" description="The core is MIT with no open-core asterisk. AI and collaboration are source-available under a commercial licence that never checks anything at runtime.">
  <Nav />
  <Legal
    kicker="Licence"
    title="MIT.<br />Actually MIT."
    lede="No open-core asterisk on the core. The framework, every built-in extension and the bindings are MIT. Two packages are commercial and say so clearly."
    updated="24 August 2026"
  >
    <h2>MIT: core, react, vue</h2>
    <p>
      The engine, document model, extension API, starter kit, tables, comments, task lists,
      table of contents, unique ids, the drag handle and Markdown. Use it commercially, modify
      it, redistribute it, no attribution UI required, no warranty.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing gets moved out of the core later to be sold back. If that ever changes, it will be
      a fork with a different name rather than a quiet edit to this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Commercial: ai, collab</h2>
    <p>
      <code>@matrajs/ai</code> and <code>@matrajs/collab</code> are source-available under the
      Matra Commercial License. Free for evaluation, development, testing, teaching, personal
      projects, registered charities, students, and internal tools at organisations with fewer
      than three developers on the codebase. Paid otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>No licence key and nothing phones home.</strong> The licence is an agreement, not
      a mechanism. You keep running the version you licensed forever, even if the subscription
      lapses — what lapses is access to new versions and to support.
    </p>

    <h2>Versions before 0.6.0</h2>
    <p>
      Every package was MIT up to and including 0.5.0, <code>ai</code> and <code>collab</code>
      included, and that grant cannot be withdrawn. If you are on 0.5.0 you may stay there under
      MIT indefinitely.
    </p>

    <h2>The full text</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/amrelaco/matra/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT licence</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/amrelaco/matra/blob/main/packages/ai/LICENSE">Commercial licence</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/amrelaco/matra/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Security model</a>
    </p>
  </Legal>
  <Footer />
</Base>
